# Trivy ignore list for the CI tooling image.
#
# Scope: this file applies to the build-time tooling image only. That image is
# never shipped, never reaches a user device, and never serves traffic. The
# dependencies that reach production are gated separately and independently by
# `npm run security:audit:prod`, which runs with --omit=dev and currently
# reports 0 critical and 0 high.
#
# Every entry carries an expiry. When it lapses, Trivy reports the finding again
# and the gate goes red until someone re-evaluates. Entries are not permitted
# without a reason and an expiry.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go standard library, compiled into the esbuild binary
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Package:       node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild
# Owner:         release-engineering
# Reason:        esbuild is a transitive devDependency of vitest via vite 6.4.3,
#                which declares esbuild ^0.25.0. 0.25.12 is already the newest
#                release in that range, so the Go stdlib cannot be advanced
#                without a vite major upgrade. Forcing an out-of-range override
#                risks breaking the build toolchain to patch a binary that never
#                ships.
# Exploitability: Build-time only. esbuild runs inside an ephemeral, non-root,
#                read-only, network-isolated CI container, over this
#                repository's own first-party source. These stdlib CVEs require
#                processing untrusted input, which does not occur here.
# Re-evaluate:   when vite is upgraded to a release accepting esbuild >= 0.26.
CVE-2025-61726 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2025-61729 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2025-68121 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-25679 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-27145 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-32280 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-32281 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-32283 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-33811 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-33814 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-39820 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-39836 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-42499 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-42504 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-56862 exp:2026-12-01

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies bundled inside npm, shipped by the pinned Node base image
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packages:      brace-expansion, ip-address, tar
# Owner:         release-engineering
# Reason:        These are npm's own vendored dependencies inside
#                node:24.20.0-bookworm-slim, which ships npm 11.19.0. They are
#                not resolvable from this repository's lockfile. Trivy reports a
#                fixed version because one exists in the ecosystem, not because
#                it can be applied here. The clean fix is a base image bump once
#                Node ships an npm with patched bundles; upgrading npm to 12.x
#                inside the image would swap the entire CI toolchain for a major
#                version to patch a build-time-only binary.
# Exploitability: Build-time only, never shipped. npm here installs from this
#                repository's own pinned lockfile, so the ReDoS, address-parsing
#                and archive-extraction paths are never fed untrusted input.
#                Production dependencies are gated separately by
#                security:audit:prod (--omit=dev), currently 0 critical, 0 high.
# Re-evaluate:   at the next Node base image bump, and no later than the expiry.
CVE-2026-14257 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-69152 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-69192 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-73566 exp:2026-11-01
